{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base and return its string representation.\n    Bases must satisfy 2 <= base < 10.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(x, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"x must be an int\")\n    if not isinstance(base, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"base must be an int\")\n    if base < 2 or base >= 10:\n        raise ValueError(\"base must be in range 2..9 (inclusive)\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    negative = x < 0\n    n = -x if negative else x\n\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        n, rem = divmod(n, base)\n        digits.append(str(rem))\n\n    result = \"\".join(reversed(digits))\n    return \"-\" + result if negative else result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the nth element of the Fib4 sequence iteratively.\n    Handles base cases for n less than 4 and uses a rolling window for larger n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the four preceding values for n=4 calculation:\n    # f_n_minus_4 corresponds to fib4(0)\n    # f_n_minus_3 corresponds to fib4(1)\n    # f_n_minus_2 corresponds to fib4(2)\n    # f_n_minus_1 corresponds to fib4(3)\n    f_n_minus_4 = 0\n    f_n_minus_3 = 0\n    f_n_minus_2 = 2\n    f_n_minus_1 = 0\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        current_fib4 = f_n_minus_1 + f_n_minus_2 + f_n_minus_3 + f_n_minus_4\n        f_n_minus_4 = f_n_minus_3\n        f_n_minus_3 = f_n_minus_2\n        f_n_minus_2 = f_n_minus_1\n        f_n_minus_1 = current_fib4\n\n    return f_n_minus_1"}
