{"task_id": "HumanEval/83", "solution": "def starts_one_ends(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts n-digit positive integers that start or end with 1.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer (n >= 1)\")\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        # For n >= 2, the count is 10^(n-1) + 9*10^(n-2) - 10^(n-2)\n        # This simplifies to 18 * 10^(n-2).\n        return 18 * (10 ** (n - 2))"}
