{"task_id": "HumanEval/132", "solution": "def is_nested(string):\n    '''\n    Checks if a string of brackets contains a nested subsequence like '[[]]'.\n    This is detected by finding two open brackets followed by two closing brackets.\n    '''\n    total_close = 0\n    for char in string:\n        if char == ']':\n            total_close += 1\n\n    seen_open = 0\n    seen_close = 0\n\n    for char in string:\n        if char == '[':\n            seen_open += 1\n            # Check if we have at least two open brackets encountered so far\n            # AND at least two closing brackets remaining in the rest of the string.\n            if seen_open >= 2 and (total_close - seen_close) >= 2:\n                return True\n        else:  # char == ']'\n            seen_close += 1\n\n    return False"}
